IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `df80-nouns`
IMPORT `df80-cross-references`

-- Row il-80. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the two items: the issue dates the footers print, what each instruction names and does, the words each printed text holds, the two replays, the two differences between a page and the consolidation, the commencements as the pages print them, the rows of the comparison table, both limbs and how each was read.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that the references are NOT complete are in df80-tests-red.l4.
-- The expected values are written from NOTES.md (the answer tables and the quotation lines), not copied from the values in df80-cross-references.l4.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- The issue dates the footers print. An issue date is NOT a commencement date.
#ASSERT `SH 464`'s `its issue date` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 7 1965)
#ASSERT `SH 508`'s `its issue date` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 8 1967)
#ASSERT `SH 548`'s `its issue date` EQUALS JUST (Date 8 1 1969)
#ASSERT `SH 1030`'s `its issue date` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 1981)
#ASSERT `the New Version`'s `its issue date` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The order of the instruments.
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 508` `SH 464`
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 548` `SH 508`
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 1030` `SH 548`
#ASSERT NOT (`the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 464` `SH 508`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the first instrument was issued after the second` `the New Version` `SH 464`)

-- The commencements as the pages print them. The Commissions of Inquiry Law prints none; the New Version prints 1 October 1968 in its section 93.
#ASSERT `the commencement of the Commissions of Inquiry Law as its pages print it`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of the New Version as section 93 prints it`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 10 1968)
#ASSERT `the commencement of the New Version as section 93 prints it`'s `the instrument`'s `its issue date` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The title forms. SH 508 item 1 prints the original title and the title it gives.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `item 1 of SH 508, the renaming of the Law` "ייקרא ״חוק איסור לשון הרע, תשכ״ה–1965״"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `item 1 of SH 508, the renaming of the Law` "חוק לשון הרע, תשכ״ה–1965 (להלן – החוק)"
#ASSERT `item 1 of SH 508, the renaming of the Law`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 133

-- I1: where each text is printed.
#ASSERT `paragraph (6) of section 13 as printed in SH 464`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `footnote 5 of printed page 242 of SH 464`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `section 30 of the Commissions of Inquiry Law as printed in SH 548`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 32
#ASSERT `footnote 9 of printed page 32 of SH 548`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 32

-- I1: what the words of paragraph (6) hold: the name, the pointer to the Basic Law, and the string the 1967 instruction names, twice.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (6) of section 13 as printed in SH 464` `the name in paragraph (6) of section 13`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (6) of section 13 as printed in SH 464` `the pointer to the Basic Law in paragraph (6)`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (6) of section 13 as printed in SH 464` (`SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the words it names`)
#ASSERT `paragraph (6), the three parts put back with the deleted string at both places` EQUALS `paragraph (6) of section 13 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`

-- I1: what SH 508 item 7 names and does.
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the kind` EQUALS `Delete words`
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the section of the Law it names` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the paragraphs it names` EQUALS LIST 5, 6
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the item` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 133
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS (`SH 508 item 7 deletes words in paragraphs (5) and (6) of section 13`'s `the words it names`) "פקודת")

-- I1: the replay of the 1967 deletion on paragraph (6), and the consolidation's words of paragraph (6). The two texts are equal (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY for the second).
#ASSERT `paragraph (6) after the 1967 deletion, replayed literally` EQUALS `the consolidation's words of paragraph (6)`
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS `paragraph (6) after the 1967 deletion, replayed literally` "ולצורך")
#ASSERT CONTAINS `paragraph (6) after the 1967 deletion, replayed literally` "בפני הועדה, או בדין"

-- I1: paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15. The page and the consolidation are two texts that differ in two places; the row types both and the differences, and gives no reason.
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) `the pointer in paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15`
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the consolidation's words of paragraph (5)(ב)` `the pointer in paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words` EQUALS `the consolidation's words of paragraph (5)(ב)`)
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) "על אפיו"
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the consolidation's words of paragraph (5)(ב)` "על אופיו"
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) "אופיו")
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS `the consolidation's words of paragraph (5)(ב)` "אפיו")
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) "עברו, מעשיו"
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the consolidation's words of paragraph (5)(ב)` "עברו מעשיו"

-- I1: the two footnotes are the same string. This is a fact about the two pages; the row says nothing more of it.
#ASSERT `footnote 5 of printed page 242 of SH 464`'s `its words` EQUALS `footnote 9 of printed page 32 of SH 548`'s `its words`

-- I1: section 30 of the 1968 Law is the one line of that Law the row reads, and its words are the name, a dash and the word בטלה.
#ASSERT `section 30 of the Commissions of Inquiry Law as printed in SH 548`'s `its words` EQUALS "פקודת ועדות חקירה – בטלה."

-- The Interpretation Law, sections 1 and 25: page facts. The words are on the pages named; nothing here evaluates them.
#ASSERT `section 1 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 302
#ASSERT `section 25 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 305
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 1 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030` "אם אין הוראה אחרת לענין הנדון"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 25 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030` "כנוסחו בשעה שנזקקים לו"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 25 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030` "והוראות שבאו במקומו בחיקוק אחר"
#ASSERT `section 25 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030`'s `the instrument that printed it`'s `its issue date` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 1981)

-- I2: where each text is printed, and what section 7 holds.
#ASSERT `section 7 as printed in SH 464`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `footnote 1 of printed page 240 of SH 464`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `the title of the New Version as printed`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 266
#ASSERT `section 93 of the New Version as printed`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 278
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD CONTAINS (`section 7 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) t) (LIST "2(2)", "15", "58", "61", "63", "68א")
#ASSERT `the numbers section 7 names after the 1967 insertion` EQUALS LIST "2(2)", "15", "55ב", "58", "61", "63", "68א"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 7 as printed in SH 464` "הסעיפים 2(2) עד 15, 58 עד 61 ו־63 עד 68א"

-- I2: what SH 508 item 4 does, and the literal replay. The two texts, the replay and the consolidation's words, differ by the comma and the space around 55ב; the row types both and the difference, and gives no reason.
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the kind` EQUALS `Insert words`
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the section of the Law it names` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the item` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 133
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the paragraphs it names` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 7, the part up to and including the characters 15` APPEND `section 7, the part after the characters 15` EQUALS `section 7 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`
#ASSERT CONTAINS `section 7 after the 1967 insertion, replayed literally` "1555ב, 58"
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the consolidation's words of section 7` "15, 55ב, 58"
#ASSERT NOT (`section 7 after the 1967 insertion, replayed literally` EQUALS `the consolidation's words of section 7`)

-- I2: the New Version's star footnote begins with the words of footnote 1 of printed page 240 of SH 464 (without its final full stop). A fact about two pages.
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`the star footnote of the New Version, printed page 266`'s `its words`) "ע״ר 1944, תוס׳ 1 מס׳ 1380, עמ׳ 93"
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`footnote 1 of printed page 240 of SH 464`'s `its words`) "ע״ר 1944, תוס׳ 1 מס׳ 1380, עמ׳ 93"

-- I2: how many rows of the comparison table are typed, and in which band.
#ASSERT count `the rows of the right-hand double column, from old 2(1) to old 15` EQUALS 22
#ASSERT count `the rows of the double column second from the left, from old 55alef to old 56` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count `the rows of the left-hand double column, from old 57 to old 71` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT count `all the rows typed from the deposited bands` EQUALS 55

-- I2: the rows for the numbers section 7 names, as data. No assertion is made on any number other than 55ב and 68א.
#ASSERT `old 2(1)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "1"
#ASSERT `old 2(2)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "2, 64 רישה"
#ASSERT `old 15`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "22"
#ASSERT `old 55alef`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "63"
#ASSERT `old 55bet(1)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "64"
#ASSERT `old 55bet(2)(alef)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "65"
#ASSERT `old 55bet(2)(bet)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "66"
#ASSERT `old 55bet(3)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "67"
#ASSERT `old 55gimel(5)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "70"
#ASSERT `old 56`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "5"
#ASSERT `old 57`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "6"
#ASSERT `old 61`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "77(א)(ב)"
#ASSERT `old 63`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "77(ג)"
#ASSERT `old 64(4)`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "85 סיפה"
#ASSERT `old 67`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "88"
#ASSERT `old 68`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "89"
#ASSERT `old 69`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "90"
#ASSERT `old 71`'s `the new-section cell` EQUALS "92"

-- I2: the position of the rows around old 68. The row for old 69 is the next row after the row for old 68, and the old-section cells of the last six rows of the left-hand band run 66, 67, 68, 69, 70, 71.
#ASSERT `old 69`'s `its place among the rows of its band` EQUALS (`old 68`'s `its place among the rows of its band`) PLUS 1
#ASSERT map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the old-section cell`) (drop 18 `the rows of the left-hand double column, from old 57 to old 71`) EQUALS LIST "66", "67", "68", "69", "70", "71"
#ASSERT `the rows printed between two rows` `old 68` `old 69` `the rows of the left-hand double column, from old 57 to old 71` EQUALS EMPTY

-- I2: the lettered old numbers the table prints, one per letter, in the band that holds them, and none in the other two bands.
#ASSERT NOT (`some row prints the letter after its old section number` "א" `the rows of the left-hand double column, from old 57 to old 71`)
#ASSERT NOT (`some row prints the letter after its old section number` "ב" `the rows of the right-hand double column, from old 2(1) to old 15`)
#ASSERT NOT (`some old-section cell contains the words` "68א" `all the rows typed from the deposited bands`)

-- The two items, with both limbs as the pages were read (NOTES.md sections 6 and 7).
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I1`
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I2`
#ASSERT `item I1`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I2`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I1`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I2`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
